WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.410 line:90%
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.345 --> 00:00:08.410 line:90%
I'm Leo Villareal.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.030 line:90%
I'm an artist based in New York.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.500 line:84%
And I've created a piece called
Light Matrix (MIT) that's

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.440 line:90%
installed for the Sloan School.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.610 line:84%
This piece consists of a
matrix of stainless steel rods.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.233 line:90%
There are 240 rods total.

00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:25.650 line:84%
So it's a three
dimensional array.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.460 line:84%
And each rod has 72 white
LEDs embedded in it.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.010 line:84%
And I have 255 levels
of brightness per LED.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.010 line:84%
The other important
component is the software.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.970 line:84%
There's a tool that
we've been working on

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:41.330 line:84%
for over 10 years that's custom
designed to create sequences.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.390 line:84%
So I'm gathering
those sequences,

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:47.002 line:84%
and then combining them into
more elaborate compositions.

00:00:47.002 --> 00:00:48.460 line:84%
And in the end,
those sequences are

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.830 line:84%
displayed in a random order
for a random amount of time.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:54.940 line:84%
I've been here working on
the fine tuning of the piece.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:55.795 line:90%
It's site specific.

00:00:55.795 --> 00:00:57.920 line:84%
So it's very important for
me to be here, you know,

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:58.962 line:90%
get a sense of the place.

00:00:58.962 --> 00:01:01.550 line:84%
So I'm looking at the
ambient light levels,

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.463 line:84%
the level of activity to find
the right tempo and brightness.

00:01:05.463 --> 00:01:07.130 line:84%
So it's really like--
almost like tuning

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.437 line:90%
a musical instrument.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.310 line:90%
Working with light is--

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.570 line:90%
I mean, it's so primal.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.190 line:84%
Light is a very
seductive material,

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.650 line:90%
so people are drawn to it.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.650 line:84%
We have this deep, as humans,
this very deep response to it.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.670 line:84%
So I'm interested in
the hypnotic qualities

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.030 line:84%
and, you know, when you're
staring into a campfire.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.840 line:84%
Tapping into that, I think,
is very powerful and something

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.780 line:90%
that you can't decode either.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.272 line:84%
I'm playing with the
compulsion pattern recognize.

00:01:36.272 --> 00:01:37.980 line:84%
You start to recognize
something but then

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.620 line:84%
it changes and becomes
something else.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.740 line:84%
It's a little bit of a game, and
that you're putting information

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.960 line:84%
out there that's
not quite complete.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.940 line:84%
But this whole process,
I think, is somehow

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.240 line:84%
pleasurable to look at
and to spend time with.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.060 line:84%
MIT's always been a sort of
mythological place for me.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.910 line:84%
And I've visited here many
times and been so inspired.

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.640 line:84%
So it's a really
great honor to be here

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:04.975 line:90%
and to work within this context.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.670 line:84%
I'm interested in the
livability of the piece,

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.860 line:84%
creating something that
can fit within the fabric

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.170 line:84%
of the architecture of
the clause of the building

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.990 line:84%
and be something that really
contributes to people's lives

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:20.870 line:90%
on campus.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.240 line:90%
And yeah.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.840 line:90%
So we'll see what happens.

